{# ============================================================================
   Motif components.  P3.1 / D2.

   Charter §5 and handoff §2 make the verification mark (✓ / ✗) THE motif, used
   relentlessly.  Defect D-14, established by cmap probe: U+2717 BALLOT X and
   U+25CF BLACK CIRCLE exist in NONE of the five shipped faces, and no X-mark
   variant exists in either family.  Left as text they fall back to a system
   symbol font — a third typeface, different on every OS, failing silently with
   all tests green.

   Director's ruling 2026-08-06 (D-14), with its added condition:
     - both marks render as a matched inline-SVG pair; ● is a CSS-drawn dot;
     - the pair renders from a SINGLE SVG source with shared stroke-weight and
       size parameters — ONE definition, TWO marks — so a future edit cannot
       drift one mark without the other;
     - the checker asserts both marks resolve from that shared definition.

   That condition is why _mark() below exists and why mark_check/mark_cross
   carry no geometry of their own: they supply a path and a name, nothing else.
   MARK_GEOMETRY is the single point of truth. build.py enforces this two ways —
   a source check that only _mark emits a mark <svg>, and a rendered-output
   check that every mark shares one viewBox and one stroke-width (MARK_DRIFT).

   Accessibility: marks are aria-hidden. Meaning is carried by adjacent text
   ("VERIFIED", "METRICS PENDING"), satisfying C-11's "no information conveyed
   by color alone" and keeping the NVDA pass (C-08) free of "check mark /
   ballot x" noise.
   ========================================================================= #}

{#- ---- THE SHARED DEFINITION. Edit these three values, both marks change. -#}
{%- set MARK_VIEWBOX = '0 0 12 12' -%}
{%- set MARK_STROKE  = '1.7' -%}
{%- set MARK_LINECAP = 'square' -%}

{%- macro _mark(kind, path, extra='') -%}
<svg class="mark mark--{{ kind }}{% if extra %} {{ extra }}{% endif %}" viewBox="{{ MARK_VIEWBOX }}" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="{{ path }}" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="{{ MARK_STROKE }}" stroke-linecap="{{ MARK_LINECAP }}"/></svg>
{%- endmacro -%}

{# The two marks: a name and a path each. No geometry, by design. #}
{% macro mark_check(extra='') -%}
{{ _mark('check', 'M1.6 6.3 4.5 9.2 10.4 3.3', extra) }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro mark_cross(extra='') -%}
{{ _mark('cross', 'M2.6 2.6 9.4 9.4M9.4 2.6 2.6 9.4', extra) }}
{%- endmacro %}

{# The version anchor + evidence link that must travel with every figure
   (contract 3.3, decision D-02). The anchor is a release tag or a commit SHA
   fetched into data/generated/github.json. It fixes the VERSION a figure was
   stated against — it never implies the figure was re-counted. #}
{% macro anchor(a, label='') -%}
<a class="anchor" href="{{ a.anchor_url }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">{% if label %}{{ label }} {% endif %}{{ a.anchor }} ↗</a>
{%- endmacro %}

{# P5.6: the record block. Two dates, named by DCMI Metadata Terms
   (https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/,
   fetched 2026-08-28):
     ISSUED   dcterms:issued   "Date of formal issuance of the resource"
              = the latest formal release of the anchored version, linked.
     MODIFIED dcterms:modified "Date on which the resource was changed"
              = the last push to the repository, fetched by the snapshot.
   Each <time datetime> carries the full ISO 8601 instant; the visible text is
   the ISO date. A repository that has never released says so. #}
{% macro record(p) -%}
<dl class="record">
  <div class="record-row">
    <dt class="mono-label">Issued</dt>
    <dd>
      {%- if p._issued_iso -%}
      <a class="anchor" href="{{ p._anchor.anchor_url }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ p._anchor.anchor }} ↗</a>
      <time class="pushed mono-meta" datetime="{{ p._issued_iso }}">{{ p._issued_date }}</time>
      {%- else -%}
      <span class="mono-meta">no release yet</span>
      <a class="anchor" href="{{ p._anchor.anchor_url }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">at {{ p._anchor.anchor }} ↗</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div class="record-row">
    <dt class="mono-label">Modified</dt>
    <dd><time class="pushed mono-meta" datetime="{{ p._pushed_iso }}">{{ p._pushed_date }}</time></dd>
  </div>
</dl>
{%- endmacro %}

{# Truth-strip live indicator. CSS-drawn; no glyph exists in either face. #}
{% macro dot(extra='') -%}
<span class="dot{% if extra %} {{ extra }}{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
{%- endmacro %}

{# A claim row's status. `state` is 'verified' or 'pending' — never a bare
   colour, so C-11 holds and the label always carries the meaning. #}
{% macro status(state, label) -%}
{%- if state == 'verified' -%}
{{ mark_check() }}<span class="status status--verified">{{ label }}</span>
{%- else -%}
{{ mark_cross() }}<span class="status status--pending">{{ label }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
